## Where the Specialists Disagree\
\
### Disagreement 1: More tools vs. fewer tools\
- **scan (gemini-3.5-flash)** and **web (gpt-5.5)** both push a maximalist stack: Figma + Playwright + Context7 + shadcn + Radix + Storybook + custom Skill.\
- **analysis (deepseek-v4-pro)** pushes back: *"A stripped-down approach: ONE CLAUDE.md file with 50 lines of design rules + the Playwright MCP for visual feedback. That's it\'85 The constraint poverty of this setup *forces intention*."*\
\
**My read:** Start minimal (CLAUDE.md + Playwright MCP). Add Figma MCP only if your Figma is well-organized. Add others only when you hit a concrete pain point. analysis has the stronger argument here because the maximalist stack has its own slop failure mode (#2 below).\
\
### Disagreement 2: Are design systems part of the solution or part of the problem?\
- **web, scan, social**: treat shadcn/ui + Radix + tokenized design systems as the antidote to slop.\
- **analysis (deepseek-v4-pro)** flags the contrarian risk: *"A heavily tokenized design system produces uniformity. Uniformity + AI generation = slop at scale\'85 Over-reliance on shadcn/ui is itself a slop vector if every site uses the same components with default styling."*\
\
**My read:** Both are right at different scales. Use shadcn/Radix for *behavior and accessibility*; override the *visual layer* with strong brand tokens that explicitly diverge from shadcn defaults. analysis's point that Airbnb/Stripe/Linear succeed by defining *where to break the system* is the synthesis.\
\
### Disagreement 3: UI-generation tools (v0 / Lovable / similar)\
- **scan (gemini-3.5-flash)**: positive \'97 "have Claude pull beautifully scaffolded, modern layouts from v0 and clean them up."\
- **analysis (deepseek-v4-pro)**: explicitly negative \'97 *"These are slop amplifiers, not reducers\'85 optimized for speed, not distinctiveness."*\
\
**My read:** analysis is more defensible. v0-style tools are trained on the same web that produces slop; they accelerate the average rather than push you off it. If you're chasing freshness, skip them.\
\
### Disagreement 4: The "Anthropic Frontend Design Skill" as flagship\
- **social (grok-4.3)**: calls it the "consensus winner."\
- **web, scan, analysis**: don't mention it.\
\
**Flag:** Three of four specialists not corroborating a "consensus winner" is suspicious. social may be picking up genuine X buzz; or it may be reflecting one community's enthusiasm for something less authoritative than presented. Verify before adopting.\
